  "body": "Builds on #341 (merged; #326, per-setup part alignment) - base `main`.\n\n## What changed\n- **App, `pick::plane` (new):** `lay_on_plane(world, picks, PlaneLay { plane, flip, place })` reads one flat face or two straight edges in the document frame and returns the setup's part alignment (rigid transform, document -> setup frame). Face: the shortest turn from the outward normal onto +Z (G17) / +Y (G18) / +X (G19), negated with Flip; the antiparallel case is a half turn about the plane's first axis (bottom onto G17 equals the \"Flip over X\" preset). Two edges: frame to frame, the plane normal onto the axis (outward = away from the parts' centre) and the first edge along X (G17/G18) or Y (G19). Turned about the parts' bounds centre like the #326 presets; \"Face to plane level\" sets the face (or the first edge's plane) to level 0 on that axis. The landing is checked (turned normal within 1e-9 rad of the axis, by the sine) before anything is returned.\n- **Command:** `AlignPartToSetup::lay_on_plane(world, setup, picks, lay)` -> `AlignPartToSetup::new` (#341's door): one undoable command, the stock follows as it does for the presets. The work offset (`setup::wcs_slot`) is never touched; rotated work offsets stay refused.\n- **Refused by name:** a curved face (patch), a degenerate face / no area, a vertex, a closed or curved edge, parallel or coincident edges, any other pick count, a pick on the stock or a fixture (\"is not the part\"), a pick no longer in the model.\n- **Shared readers:** `pick::align`'s outward-normal and straight-edge readers take the frame as a parameter (3-2-1 keeps the active setup's view; behaviour unchanged).\n- **UI:** each Setups page row gets \"Lay on a plane\": *Pick face or edges* (arms a view-state draft `State::plane_pick` + Edge mode, so edges and faces both pick; a face replaces the draft, an edge toggles and keeps the last two; draft picks drawn in the violet pick outline), G17/G18/G19 combo, *Flip*, *Face to plane level*, *Apply* (enabled only when the app reads the picks as a plane; the disabled tooltip says why). Apply queues `CommandKind::LayPartOnPlane`; only Apply is a command.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/330-pick-to-plane.md` (absolute in the document frame; row's setup; no-setup = no row, matching #341; edge outward rule; tolerances).\n\n## Readings\n- New suite `plane_align`: 9 passed. Normal within 1e-9 rad of each target axis for G17/G18/G19 x flip, on a square block and a block tilted (20, 35, -50) deg; edges: first edge along the plane's first axis within 1e-9 rad; place-on-level: wall corners at level 0 within 1e-7 mm.\n- App: setup_align 8, pick 9, wcs_align 5, commands_undo 32, project_roundtrip 68, golden_cl 23 - all pass.\n- UI lib (CWD crates/ui): 293 passed, 2 ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- `plane_align`: `a_face_lands_its_outward_normal_on_each_plane_axis`, `the_bottom_onto_g17_is_a_flip_over_x_about_the_centre`, `place_on_level_sets_the_face_onto_the_plane`, `two_edges_set_the_plane_and_the_first_one_runs_along_its_first_axis`, `the_command_writes_the_setup_alignment_and_undo_restores_it`, `a_second_setup_lays_a_different_face_down`, `the_top_face_onto_g17_is_already_how_the_part_sits`, `every_pick_that_sets_no_plane_is_refused_by_name`, `a_curved_face_and_a_curved_edge_are_refused_by_name`\n- ui `egui_app::setup_plane_tests`: `the_row_picks_a_face_and_lays_it_on_g17_through_the_command`, `edge_picks_keep_the_last_two_and_parallel_edges_push_nothing`\n\nNot covered by a test: the degenerate-face refusal (feature detection gives no easy fixture for a `FaceKind::Degenerate` face; the code path is guarded) and the viewport ray routing into the draft (the test feeds `plane_pick::take` directly).\n\nChangelog: Setups page: lay the part on a G17/G18/G19 plane by picking a flat face or two straight edges (flip, optional face to plane level), undoable, written as the setup's part alignment\n\nFixes #330\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
